{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_8e51539aaeea4b72ae26d08d8d7198f1","id":"pg_93a669d6036c5431a4349f3244c727eb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-nexus-guard-aip-requirements-txt-3d8c873139ea-9f3244c727eb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_90b7fe34a3c25d988bec09b69a4732a1"],"title":"The-Nexus-Guard/aip/requirements.txt @ 3d8c873139ea","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8e51539aaeea4b72ae26d08d8d7198f1"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3715f251fceb5812b75246e44ef07b0f02bfd974d74f356d5ccfb1d01d6fbb00"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AIP targets agent-to-agent security gaps: verifying who an agent is, deciding trustworthiness via vouch chains, signing skills for code provenance, and private messaging, including MCP and A2A protocol integrations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_612a45aec8782e67978dbf64daa8d4cb5e87536f369ad477b92e75110922e0ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A CLI named 'aip' exposes commands including init, register, verify, vouch, revoke, sign, message, messages, reply, rotate-key, trust-score, trust-graph, doctor, export, import, search, and cache."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65b86f13998ec396cca9bb073d7e369a1f2960beddc417ed6699eaca8820a199"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A pure-Python implementation exists with zero dependencies; optional performance dependencies include cryptography or pynacl, and langchain-core is an optional dependency for framework tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69941c125971d2e5c56fd8abb934dd0c71702f1049b279f9d40d4f9878707724"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The protocol is designed to be decentralized with no central registry, local-first so each agent keeps its own trust view, and auditable via signed 'isnad' trust chains."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba7db7ae40652595d077e6138ae6ac1a97d039c1984ae8a81d7d2ea32bb8af37"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Message signing uses the payload format sender_did|recipient_did|timestamp|encrypted_content; the older format without encrypted_content still works but is deprecated and slated for removal."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c7792ef0f183a74aa8ce2b5b8d55e63032db8e712c5919c3d0b2576a4cff8e02"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Trust paths use decay scoring across hops (e.g., a documented example of 0.64 for two hops at 0.8 decay), and badges turn green 'Verified' at 3+ CODE_SIGNING vouches."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8161a12388fd119441499c2afc79faee98109dfed98008c618fd30f334addbe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An identity middleware (AIPMiddleware) signs outgoing HTTP requests and verifies incoming ones, exposing trust-score-gated processing and peer discovery by minimum trust."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0a97f31febeb14bd0df7911e4774f70f7c7b41fe550626bd9992f08889f46d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The status checklist marks trust gossip protocol and reputation scoring as unchecked, indicating these are not yet implemented in v0.5.46."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8d132b6b3202243fe667dc83b212702ae75f1ac3c533ef13766dde48ff432aa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AIP is organized into three layers: an identity layer (Ed25519 keypairs, DIDs, challenge-response), a trust layer (vouches, scopes, paths, revocation), and a communication layer (E2E encrypted messaging)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f99fa7e0d037e1fad8f722297072e61ca507bcc86627f8b0c7b9f99720b34b4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README points contributors to a Contributing Guide and GitHub Discussions for questions and ideas."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3715f251fceb5812b75246e44ef07b0f02bfd974d74f356d5ccfb1d01d6fbb00","clm_612a45aec8782e67978dbf64daa8d4cb5e87536f369ad477b92e75110922e0ef","clm_65b86f13998ec396cca9bb073d7e369a1f2960beddc417ed6699eaca8820a199","clm_69941c125971d2e5c56fd8abb934dd0c71702f1049b279f9d40d4f9878707724","clm_ba7db7ae40652595d077e6138ae6ac1a97d039c1984ae8a81d7d2ea32bb8af37","clm_c7792ef0f183a74aa8ce2b5b8d55e63032db8e712c5919c3d0b2576a4cff8e02","clm_c8161a12388fd119441499c2afc79faee98109dfed98008c618fd30f334addbe","clm_d0a97f31febeb14bd0df7911e4774f70f7c7b41fe550626bd9992f08889f46d2","clm_f8d132b6b3202243fe667dc83b212702ae75f1ac3c533ef13766dde48ff432aa","clm_f99fa7e0d037e1fad8f722297072e61ca507bcc86627f8b0c7b9f99720b34b4a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_8e51539aaeea4b72ae26d08d8d7198f1","id":"pg_ad1973a4aa0a535892463214f1ffb871","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-nexus-guard-aip-readme-md-3d8c873139ea-3214f1ffb871.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_383914975aaf5cbbbb09ab19317e0008"],"title":"The-Nexus-Guard/aip/README.md @ 3d8c873139ea","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:10:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8e51539aaeea4b72ae26d08d8d7198f1"}
